{"abstract":"Mentoring is a key component of scientific achievements, contributing to overall measures of career success for mentees and mentors. Within the scientific community, possessing a large research group is often perceived as an indicator of exceptional mentorship and high-quality research. However, such large, competitive groups may also escalate dropout rates, particularly among early-career researchers. Overly high dropout rates of young researchers may lead to severe postdoc shortage and loss of top-tier academics in contemporary academia. In this context, we collect longitudinal genealogical data on mentor-mentee relations and their publications, and analyse the influence of a mentor's group size on the future academic longevity and performance of their mentees. Our findings indicate that mentees trained in larger groups tend to exhibit superior academic performance compared with those from smaller groups, provided they remain in academia post graduation. However, we also observe two surprising patterns: academic survival rate is significantly lower for (1) mentees from larger groups and for (2) mentees with more productive mentors. The trend is verified in institutions of different prestige levels. These findings highlight a negative correlation between a mentor's success and the academic survival rate of their mentees, prompting a rethinking of effective mentorship and offering actionable insights for career advancement.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Xing, Yanmeng","Ma, Yifang","Fan, Ying","Sinatra, Roberta","Zeng, An"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-819204"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Beijing Normal University","Southern University of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["Commitment","Mentorship","Networks","PhD","Science","Scientific careers"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"academic mentees thrive in big groups but survive in small groups","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-819204","identifier":[{"id":"001435527900001","type":"wos"},{"id":"86000308059","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40033134","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-5e1a7bbf-3470-4b0c-bda7-6a977641d9f6"],"keyword":["Commitment","Mentorship","Networks","Phd","Science","Scientific careers"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-CF0D28C8273C9FA4B431F86344C1998A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"beijing normal university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Beijing Normal University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"southern university of science and technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Southern University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, SODAS, SODAS"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","first":"Yanmeng","key":"xingpau","last":"Xing","name":"Xing, Yanmeng","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Yifang","key":"mapau","last":"Ma","name":"Ma, Yifang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ying","key":"fanpau","last":"Fan","name":"Fan, Ying","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Roberta","key":"sinatrapau","last":"Sinatra","locid":"df859e44-cb2b-41f8-b85b-cfd243c37ab2","name":"Sinatra, Roberta","orcid":"0000-0002-7558-1028","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"An","key":"zengpau","last":"Zeng","name":"Zeng, An","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40033134"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41562-025-02114-8","issn":["23973374"],"journal":"Nature Human Behaviour","pages":"902-916","status":"p","title":"Nature Human Behaviour","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-86000308059"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5e1a7bbf-3470-4b0c-bda7-6a977641d9f6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Academic mentees thrive in big groups, but survive in small groups","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-819204","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Success in sports is a complex phenomenon that has only garnered limited research attention. In particular, we lack a deep scientific understanding of success in sports like tennis and the factors that contribute to it. Here, we study the unfolding of tennis players’ careers to understand the role of early career stages and the impact of specific tournaments on players’ trajectories. We employ a comprehensive approach combining network science and analysis of the Association of Tennis Professionals (ATP) tournament data and introduce a novel method to quantify tournament prestige based on the eigenvector centrality of the co-attendance network of tournaments. Focusing on the interplay between participation in central tournaments and players’ performance, we find that the level of the tournament where players achieve their first win is associated with becoming a top player. This work sheds light on the critical role of the initial stages in the progression of players’ careers, offering valuable insights into the dynamics of success in tennis.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Zappalà, Chiara","Sousa, Sandro","Cunha, Tiago","Pluchino, Alessandro","Rapisarda, Andrea","Sinatra, Roberta"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-739093"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Hungary","Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Complexity Science Hub Vienna","Corvinus University of Budapest","National Institute for Nuclear Physics"],"keyword":["Sports analytics","Success"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"early career wins and tournament prestige characterize tennis players trajectories","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1140/epjds/s13688-024-00472-3","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-739093","identifier":[{"id":"001205282000001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85190789694","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-5191a843-bb69-40e4-ae2f-b252af5c8dd1"],"keyword":["Network science applications","Sports analytics","Success"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8B680870714C22EC2FCC9E82D13074A7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1140/epjds/s13688-024-00472-3","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/391117020/Early_career_wins.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"hu","key":"corvinus university of budapest","loc":["Hungary","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Corvinus University of Budapest","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"national institute for nuclear physics","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"National Institute for Nuclear Physics","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"at","key":"complexity science hub vienna","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Complexity Science Hub Vienna","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3 4","first":"Chiara","key":"zappalàpau","last":"Zappalà","name":"Zappalà, Chiara","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Sandro","key":"sousapau","last":"Sousa","name":"Sousa, Sandro","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Tiago","key":"cunhapau","last":"Cunha","name":"Cunha, Tiago","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Alessandro","key":"pluchinopau","last":"Pluchino","name":"Pluchino, Alessandro","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 5","first":"Andrea","key":"rapisardapau","last":"Rapisarda","name":"Rapisarda, Andrea","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Roberta","key":"sinatrapau","last":"Sinatra","locid":"df859e44-cb2b-41f8-b85b-cfd243c37ab2","name":"Sinatra, Roberta","orcid":"0000-0002-7558-1028","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1140/epjds/s13688-024-00472-3","issn":["21931127"],"issue":"1","journal":"EPJ Data Science","paperid":"32","status":"p","title":"EPJ Data Science","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85190789694"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5191a843-bb69-40e4-ae2f-b252af5c8dd1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Early career wins and tournament prestige characterize tennis players’ trajectories","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-739093","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The Physics Nobel Prize was awarded to the groundbreaking research of John Hopfield and Geoffrey Hinton on artificial neural networks. This surprised many scientists and caused dissenting opinions, as this topic is commonly perceived as Computer Science - So why the prize in Physics? Instead of relying on opinions, there are robust, data-driven methods from Science of Science to contextualize this award using citation data. This way, we have shown that indeed ``Hopfield's 1982 paper on neural networks [is] indistinguishable from papers published in physics journals'', similar to ``six physics Nobel winning publications'' in interdisciplinary physics. Further, we assessed that interdisciplinary papers like Hopfield's and Hinton's are ripe for a Nobel Prize: Until recently, the Physics Nobel Prize has been used to award traditional physics research impacting physics only; this year's award however shows that the prize has caught up with reality, recognizing interdisciplinary discoveries that impact both physics and other fields. We are hopeful that this recognition will expedite the breakup of disciplinary silos which obstruct out-of-the-box thinking that combines ideas from different disciplines. This breakup is urgently needed to solve the world's big challenges like climate change. Physics itself is undergoing extensive changes and ``spin-offs'', influencing emerging fields like data science that embrace interdisciplinarity. In contrast, clinging to research fields as fixed territories is at best small-minded, at worst harmful. Although we should not discard useful domain knowledge, there is a clear need for better use of data and breaking up silo mentalities.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Szell, Michael","Ma, Yifang","Sinatra, Roberta"],"cuid":["S02-085.09-804389"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Northwestern University","Southern University of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["Machine learning","Physics","Scientific community"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"was the nobel prize for physics yes not that it matters","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/107042248/szell2024wnp.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S02-085.09-804389","identifier":[{"id":"001344642400002","type":"wos"},{"id":"85207502283","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39438749","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["itu-12c76d0b-1461-4612-b998-c55df87095b5","ku-bfac9f0f-d7a9-4b98-9516-3475a8988ab9"],"keyword":["Machine learning","Physics","Scientific community"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-BE7ABFCE3BEFDE2E986E4ED139FF5606"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/107042248/szell2024wnp.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"northwestern university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Northwestern University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"southern university of science and technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Southern University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, SODAS, SODAS"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"szellpau","last":"Szell","locid":"2ef641d0-bd79-425b-8b12-b58d74b993ae","name":"Szell, Michael","orcid":"0000-0003-3022-2483","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Yifang","key":"mapau","last":"Ma","name":"Ma, Yifang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Roberta","key":"sinatrapau","last":"Sinatra","locid":"418f030f-2b26-4c74-a77b-c0c87d13f56d","name":"Sinatra, Roberta","orcid":"0000-0002-7558-1028","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39438749"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/d41586-024-03435-w","issn":["00280836","14764687"],"issn_org":["00280836"],"issue":"8035","journal":"Nature","pages":"782-782","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Nature","volume":"634"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-12c76d0b-1461-4612-b998-c55df87095b5","ku-bfac9f0f-d7a9-4b98-9516-3475a8988ab9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Was the Nobel prize for physics? Yes - not that it matters","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-085.09-804389","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In recent years, Danish child protective services have experienced increasing pressure, prompting the adoption of a decision-support algorithm to aid caseworkers in identifying children at heightened risk of maltreatment, named Decision Support. Despite its critical role, this algorithm has not undergone formal evaluation. Through a freedom of information request, we were able to partially access the algorithm and conduct an audit. We find that the algorithm has significant methodological flaws, suffers from information leakage, relies on inappropriate proxy values for maltreatment assessment, generates inconsistent risk scores, and exhibits age-based discrimination. Given these serious issues, we strongly advise against the use of this kind of algorithms in local government, municipal, and child protection settings, and we call for rigorous evaluation of such tools before implementation and for continual monitoring post-deployment by listing a series of specific recommendations.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Hansen, Therese Moreau","Sinatra, Roberta","Sekara, Vedran"],"cuid":["S02-089.68-804393"],"event":{"end":"2024-06-06","place":"Rio de Janeiro, br","start":"2024-06-03","title":"6th ACM Conference on Fairness, Accountability, and Transparency (ACM FAccT)","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Algorithmic audit","Algorithmic decision making","Algorithmic discrimination","Technological fairness"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"failing our youngest on the biases pitfalls and risks in a decision support algorithm used for child protection","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3630106.3658906","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-089.68-804393","identifier":[{"id":"001253359300021","type":"wos"},{"id":"85196637869","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-64a51310-bbb8-4cf4-8ca1-b9697f8426e7","ku-cec9c397-f29c-4627-9362-93ba74e9ea4d"],"keyword":["Algorithmic audit","Algorithmic decision making","Algorithmic discrimination","Technological fairness"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-DF5FB5A3B7E76B0C59F3D88F5EF61E1F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3630106.3658906","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Therese Moreau","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Therese Moreau","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Roberta","key":"sinatrapau","last":"Sinatra","locid":"418f030f-2b26-4c74-a77b-c0c87d13f56d","name":"Sinatra, Roberta","orcid":"0000-0002-7558-1028","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vedran","key":"sekarapau","last":"Sekara","locid":"db64c222-0674-4eab-9f09-7f9ea1c483e3","name":"Sekara, Vedran","orcid":"0000-0003-4490-3757","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3630106.3658906","eisbn":["9798400704505"],"pages":"290-300","publisher":"Assoc Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings Of The 2024 Acm Conference On Fairness, Accountability, And Transparency, Acm Facct 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85196637869"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-64a51310-bbb8-4cf4-8ca1-b9697f8426e7","ku-cec9c397-f29c-4627-9362-93ba74e9ea4d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Failing Our Youngest: On the Biases, Pitfalls, and Risks in a Decision Support Algorithm Used for Child Protection","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-089.68-804393","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This CPH Tech Policy Brief is based on a working paper by Vedran Sekara, Therese Moreau Hansen and Roberta Sinatra. The brief provides a small introduction to algorithmic fairness and an example of auditing fairness in an algorithm which was aimed at identifying and assessing children at risk from abuse.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Sekara, Vedran","Thorsen, Tess Sophie Skadegård","Sinatra, Roberta"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718900"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Algorithmic fairness","Artificial intelligence","Machine learning"],"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Danish Pioneer Centre for AI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"algorithmic fairness learnings from a case that used ai for decision support","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://marycenter.ku.dk/netvaerk/cph-tech-policy-committee/cph-tech-policy-brief-6/CPH_TECH_POLICY_BRIEF_no._6.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718900","ids":["itu-a0a6e2fb-fce4-46da-bc3f-7c0f11eae058"],"keyword":["Algorithmic Fairness","Artificial Intelligence","Machine Learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4515E88101983D86E40A43D547F9B7D7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://marycenter.ku.dk/netvaerk/cph-tech-policy-committee/cph-tech-policy-brief-6/CPH_TECH_POLICY_BRIEF_no._6.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Danish Pioneer Centre for AI"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vedran","key":"sekarapau","last":"Sekara","locid":"db64c222-0674-4eab-9f09-7f9ea1c483e3","name":"Sekara, Vedran","orcid":"0000-0003-4490-3757","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tess Sophie Skadegård","key":"thorsenpau","last":"Thorsen","name":"Thorsen, Tess Sophie Skadegård","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Roberta","key":"sinatrapau","last":"Sinatra","locid":"418f030f-2b26-4c74-a77b-c0c87d13f56d","name":"Sinatra, Roberta","orcid":"0000-0002-7558-1028","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"5","status":"p","volume":"CPH Tech Policy Brief"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a0a6e2fb-fce4-46da-bc3f-7c0f11eae058"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Algorithmic Fairness: Learnings From a Case That Used AI For Decision Support","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718900","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Sammen med panelet dykker Christiane Vejlø ned i de digitale blinde vinkler og undersøger den data der mangler – eller ligefrem er usynlig. Del og Like er en podcast om de digitale dilemmaer, som vi alle forholder os til i hverdagen. Den er lavet i samarbejde med ADD projektet.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Viemose, Rikke","Flyverbom, Mikkel","Sinatra, Roberta","Vejlø, Christiane","Birck, Ninette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-295434"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Viemose Media"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"usynlige kvinder med livet som indsats del amp like 000000000006","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dnt","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://open.spotify.com/episode/1agxjmJlSQL3LOOxihEeST","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-295434","ids":["cbs-d2b065fb-63db-4d2a-a38f-92ffcabb6840"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-0FC6B132B3F44FE1DF00AC39BBDA657C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://spreaker.page.link/?link=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.spreaker.com%2Fepisode%2F49827585%3Futm_medium%3Dapp%26utm_source%3Dwidget%26utm_campaign%3Depisode-title&apn=com.spreaker.android&ibi=com.spreaker.Spreaker&ius=spreaker&isi=388449677","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://open.spotify.com/episode/1agxjmJlSQL3LOOxihEeST","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Viemose Media"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Management, Society and Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke","key":"viemosepau","last":"Viemose","name":"Viemose, Rikke","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikkel","key":"flyverbompau","last":"Flyverbom","locid":"85ddabd4-7915-496a-81e1-41610119ef88","name":"Flyverbom, Mikkel","orcid":"0000-0001-9465-6219","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Roberta","key":"sinatrapau","last":"Sinatra","name":"Sinatra, Roberta","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christiane","key":"vejløpau","last":"Vejlø","name":"Vejlø, Christiane","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ninette","key":"birckppu","last":"Birck","name":"Birck, Ninette","rank":5,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Elektronista","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-d2b065fb-63db-4d2a-a38f-92ffcabb6840"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Usynlige kvinder – Med livet som indsats : Del &amp; Like #6","type":"Non-Textual Item","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-295434","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Cycling is a promising solution to unsustainable urban transport systems. However, prevailing bicycle network development follows a slow and piecewise process, without taking into account the structural complexity of transportation networks. Here we explore systematically the topological limitations of urban bicycle network development. For 62 cities we study different variations of growing a synthetic bicycle network between an arbitrary set of points routed on the urban street network. We find initially decreasing returns on investment until a critical threshold, posing fundamental consequences to sustainable urban planning: cities must invest into bicycle networks with the right growth strategy, and persistently, to surpass a critical mass. We also find pronounced overlaps of synthetically grown networks in cities with well-developed existing bicycle networks, showing that our model reflects reality. Growing networks from scratch makes our approach a generally applicable starting point for sustainable urban bicycle network planning with minimal data requirements.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Szell, Michael","Mimar, Sayat","Perlman, Tyler","Ghoshal, Gourab","Sinatra, Roberta"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-673005"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Italy","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Complexity Science Hub Vienna","Institute for Scientific Interchange Foundation","University of Rochester"],"keyword":["Bicycle networks","Network growth strategy","Sustainable planning","Transportation infrastructure","Urban transportation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"growing urban bicycle networks","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-022-10783-y","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-673005","identifier":[{"id":"85128959593","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35474086","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9039277","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["itu-d3ed33d8-cda0-424f-9f44-c048d64586ff","ku-bb213ba6-ec98-4845-9b60-54adb769800e"],"keyword":["Bicycle networks","Network growth strategy","Sustainable planning","Transportation infrastructure","Urban transportation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-4FE0AE365306E2A94A24193984AF3997"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/347002407/s41598_022_10783_y.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86710417/szell2022gub.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-022-10783-y","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of rochester","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Rochester","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Faculty of Social Sciences, shared expenditure, Social Data Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"szellpau","last":"Szell","locid":"2ef641d0-bd79-425b-8b12-b58d74b993ae","name":"Szell, Michael","orcid":"0000-0003-3022-2483","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sayat","key":"mimarpau","last":"Mimar","name":"Mimar, Sayat","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Tyler","key":"perlmanpau","last":"Perlman","name":"Perlman, Tyler","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Gourab","key":"ghoshalpau","last":"Ghoshal","name":"Ghoshal, Gourab","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","first":"Roberta","key":"sinatrapau","last":"Sinatra","locid":"df859e44-cb2b-41f8-b85b-cfd243c37ab2","name":"Sinatra, Roberta","orcid":"0000-0002-7558-1028","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35474086"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-022-10783-y","issn":["20452322"],"issue":"6765","journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"6765","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85128959593"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d3ed33d8-cda0-424f-9f44-c048d64586ff","ku-bb213ba6-ec98-4845-9b60-54adb769800e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Growing urban bicycle networks","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-673005","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Luck is considered a crucial ingredient to achieve impact in all creative domains,despite their diversity. For instance, in science, the movie industry, music, and art, theoccurrence of the highest impact work and a hot streak within a creative career arevery difficult to predict. Are there domains that are more prone to luck than others?Here, we provide new insights on the role of randomness in impact in creative careersin two ways: (i) we systematically untangle luck and individual ability to generateimpact in the movie, music, and book industries, and in science, and compare theluck factor between these fields; (ii) we show the surprising presence of randomnessin the relationship between collaboration networks and timing of career hits. Takentogether, our analysis suggests that luck consistently affects career impact across allconsidered sectors and improves our understanding in pinpointing the key elementsin driving success.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Janosov, Milán","Battiston, Federico","Sinatra, Roberta"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381374"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Hungary"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Central European University"],"keyword":["Creative careers","Dynamics of impact","Science of science","Success"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"success and luck in creative careers","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1140/epjds/s13688-020-00227-w","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381374","identifier":[{"id":"85083994297","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-07b4c815-7a38-4fa9-b82f-16991bb4caab"],"keyword":["Creative careers","Dynamics of impact","Science of science","Success"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B9E62AD656DFB6857BDD3CA37F05C73F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1140/epjds/s13688-020-00227-w","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85284865/Janosov_et_al_2020_EPJ_Data_Science.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"hu","key":"central european university","loc":["Hungary","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Central European University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Milán","key":"janosovpau","last":"Janosov","name":"Janosov, Milán","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Federico","key":"battistonpau","last":"Battiston","name":"Battiston, Federico","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Roberta","key":"sinatrapau","last":"Sinatra","locid":"418f030f-2b26-4c74-a77b-c0c87d13f56d","name":"Sinatra, Roberta","orcid":"0000-0002-7558-1028","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1140/epjds/s13688-020-00227-w","issn":["21931127"],"journal":"EPJ Data Science","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"EPJ Data Science","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85083994297"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-07b4c815-7a38-4fa9-b82f-16991bb4caab"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Success and luck in creative careers","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381374","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"There is extensive, yet fragmented, evidence of gender differences in academia suggesting that women are underrepresented in most scientific disciplines and publish fewer articles throughout a career, and their work acquires fewer citations. Here, we offer a comprehensive picture of longitudinal gender differences in performance through a bibliometric analysis of academic publishing careers by reconstructing the complete publication history of over 1.5 million gender-identified authors whose publishing career ended between 1955 and 2010, covering 83 countries and 13 disciplines. We find that, paradoxically, the increase of participation of women in science over the past 60 years was accompanied by an increase of gender differences in both productivity and impact. Most surprisingly, though, we uncover two gender invariants, finding that men and women publish at a comparable annual rate and have equivalent career-wise impact for the same size body of work. Finally, we demonstrate that differences in publishing career lengths and dropout rates explain a large portion of the reported career-wise differences in productivity and impact, although productivity differences still remain. This comprehensive picture of gender inequality in academia can help rephrase the conversation around the sustainability of women’s careers in academia, with important consequences for institutions and policy makers.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Huang, Junming","Gates, Alexander J.","Sinatra, Roberta","Barabási, Albert-László"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382689"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["China","Hungary","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Central European University","Harvard Medical School","Northeastern University","Princeton University","University of Electronic Science and Technology of China"],"keyword":["Gender inequality","STEM","Science of science","Scientific careers"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"historical comparison of gender inequality in scientific careers across countries and disciplines","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1914221117","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382689","identifier":[{"id":"85081131069","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-5eb99b52-5d35-4d56-bfe6-8f594d3fb06b"],"keyword":["STEM","gender inequality","science of science","scientific careers"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8440818180DAC1B5C6113213CF1696FD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1914221117","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85323153/sinatra_huang_gender_PNAS.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"northeastern university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Northeastern University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"university of electronic science and technology of china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Electronic Science and Technology of China","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"princeton university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Princeton University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"hu","key":"central european university","loc":["Hungary","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Central European University","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"us","key":"harvard medical school","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Harvard Medical School","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Junming","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Junming","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander J.","key":"gatespau","last":"Gates","name":"Gates, Alexander J.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Roberta","key":"sinatrapau","last":"Sinatra","locid":"418f030f-2b26-4c74-a77b-c0c87d13f56d","name":"Sinatra, Roberta","orcid":"0000-0002-7558-1028","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5 6","corresponding":null,"first":"Albert-László","key":"barabásipau","last":"Barabási","name":"Barabási, Albert-László","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1073/pnas.1914221117","issn":["00278424","10916490"],"issn_org":["00278424"],"issue":"9","journal":"Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America","pages":"4609-4616","publisher":"The National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America","volume":"117"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85081131069"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5eb99b52-5d35-4d56-bfe6-8f594d3fb06b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Historical comparison of gender inequality in scientific careers across countries and disciplines","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382689","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Novelty indicators are increasingly important for science policy. This paper challenges the indicators of novelty as an atypical combination of knowledge (Uzzi et al., 2013) and as the first appearance of a knowledge combination (Wang et al., 2017). We exploit a sample of 230,854 articles (1985 - 2005), published on 8 journals of the American Physical Society (APS) and 2.4 million citations to test the indicators using (i) a Configuration Null Model, (ii) an external validation set of articles related to Nobel Prize winning researches and APS Milestones, (iii) a set of established interdisciplinarity indicators, and (iv) the relationship with the articles’ impact. We find that novelty as the first appearance of a knowledge combination captures the key structural properties of the citation network and finds it difficult to tell novel and non-novel articles apart, while novelty as an atypical combination of knowledge overlaps with interdisciplinarity. We suggest that the policy evidence derived from these measures should be reassessed.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Fontana, Magda","Iori, Martina","Montobbio, Fabio","Sinatra, Roberta"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382056"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bocconi University","Catholic University of the Sacred Heart","Collegio Carlo Alberto","Sant'Anna School of Advanced Studies","University of Turin"],"keyword":["IMPACT","Indicator","Interdisciplinarity","Novelty","Physics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"new and atypical combinations an assessment of novelty and interdisciplinarity","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85284818/researchpolicy_sinatra.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382056","identifier":[{"id":"85087275399","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-35b4d241-93c2-43b6-b843-c38920d8487a"],"keyword":["Impact","Indicator","Interdisciplinarity","Novelty","Physics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-17C4C5410931356C0E32ACE2BCEB8083"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85284818/researchpolicy_sinatra.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"university of turin","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Turin","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"sant anna school of advanced studies","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Sant'Anna School of Advanced Studies","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"catholic university of the sacred heart","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Catholic University of the Sacred Heart","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"it","key":"bocconi university","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Bocconi University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"it","key":"collegio carlo alberto","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Collegio Carlo Alberto","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Magda","key":"fontanapau","last":"Fontana","name":"Fontana, Magda","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Martina","key":"ioripau","last":"Iori","name":"Iori, Martina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabio","key":"montobbiopau","last":"Montobbio","name":"Montobbio, Fabio","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Roberta","key":"sinatrapau","last":"Sinatra","locid":"418f030f-2b26-4c74-a77b-c0c87d13f56d","name":"Sinatra, Roberta","orcid":"0000-0002-7558-1028","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.respol.2020.104063","issn":["00487333"],"issue":"7","journal":"Research Policy","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Research Policy","volume":"49"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087275399"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-35b4d241-93c2-43b6-b843-c38920d8487a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"New and atypical combinations: An assessment of novelty and interdisciplinarity","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382056","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"This paper examines visitors’ sequential movements and their patterns in a large-scale art museum. Visitors’ available time makes their visiting styles different, resulting in dissimilarity in the order and number of visited places and in path sequence length. Since the probability of the appearance of short combinations of nodes is higher than that of long combinations of nodes, shorter path sequences tend to appear more frequently than longer path sequences. This prevents us from evaluating the strength of visitors’ mobility patterns, independent of their path sequence length. In order to solve this problem, we propose the random walk simulation model and compare the results with observed data. A random walk is a minimalistic model providing a reference line for the frequency of sequences as induced by the graph structure of the museum. The random walk simulations can therefore provide us with the probability of transitions between nodes and hence with the probability of each path of a given length. Thus, it enables us to compare the frequency of different path sequence lengths in the same framework. Our results indicate that short-stay visitors exhibit stronger patterns than long-stay visitors, confirming that short-stay visitors are more selective than long-stay visitors in terms of their visiting style. This is suggestive of the informal learning settings in which visitors shape their experiences through exploration in space.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Yoshimura, Yuji","Sinatra, Roberta","Krebs, Anne","Ratti, Carlo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384761"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Dominique-Vivant Denon Research Centre","Massachusetts Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Museum","Random walk model","Visitor studies","architectural intent","curatorial intent"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"analysis of visitors mobility patterns through random walk in the louvre museum","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84519931/AIHC2019_preprint.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-384761","identifier":[{"id":"85072053617","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ed03df98-dc84-4868-b4d4-e67534f221f8"],"keyword":["architectural intent","curatorial intent","museum","random walk model","visitor studies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9C5D9A4BB1E82C6D1BF4BC0601E5239E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84519931/AIHC2019_preprint.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"massachusetts institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Massachusetts Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"fr","key":"dominique vivant denon research centre","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Dominique-Vivant Denon Research Centre","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuji","key":"yoshimurapau","last":"Yoshimura","name":"Yoshimura, Yuji","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Roberta","key":"sinatrapau","last":"Sinatra","locid":"418f030f-2b26-4c74-a77b-c0c87d13f56d","name":"Sinatra, Roberta","orcid":"0000-0002-7558-1028","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne","key":"krebspau","last":"Krebs","name":"Krebs, Anne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carlo","key":"rattipau","last":"Ratti","name":"Ratti, Carlo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s12652-019-01428-6","issn":["18685137","18685145"],"issn_org":["18685137"],"journal":"Journal of Ambient Intelligence and Humanized Computing","pages":"1-16","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Journal of Ambient Intelligence and Humanized Computing"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85072053617"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ed03df98-dc84-4868-b4d4-e67534f221f8"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Analysis of visitors’ mobility patterns through random walk in the Louvre Museum","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384761","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Identifying fundamental drivers of science and developing predictive models to capture its evolution are instrumental for the design of policies that can improve the scientific enterprise-for example, through enhanced career paths for scientists, better performance evaluation for organizations hosting research, discovery of novel effective funding vehicles, and even identification of promising regions along the scientific frontier. The science of science uses large-scale data on the production of science to search for universal and domain-specific patterns. Here, we review recent developments in this transdisciplinary field.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Fortunato, Santo","Bergstrom, Carl T.","Börner, Katy","Evans, James A.","Helbing, Dirk","Milojević, Staša","Petersen, Alexander M.","Radicchi, Filippo","Sinatra, Roberta","Uzzi, Brian","Vespignani, Alessandro","Waltman, Ludo","Wang, Dashun","Barabási, Albert László"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-701772"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Italy","Netherlands","Switzerland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Central European University","Dana-Farber Cancer Institute","ETH Zürich","Indiana University Bloomington","Institute for Scientific Interchange Foundation","Leiden University","Northeastern University","Northwestern University","The University of Chicago","University of California Merced","University of Washington"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"science of science","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aao0185","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-701772","identifier":[{"id":"85042855814","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29496846","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-656112e6-171d-4f96-a6d9-9a7620e0d88c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8916B0A5C757E493A36939759E630796"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aao0185","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"indiana university bloomington","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Indiana University Bloomington","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of washington","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Washington","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"the university of chicago","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"The University of Chicago","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ch","key":"eth zürich","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"ETH Zürich","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"university of california merced","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California Merced","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Faculty of Social Sciences, shared expenditure, Social Data Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"us","key":"northwestern university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Northwestern University","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"us","key":"northeastern university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Northeastern University","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"it","key":"institute for scientific interchange foundation","loc":["Italy","Europe,